    "result_text": "Build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented for **owner identity version 2**.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** (new `IdentityVersion` helper, `TAG = \"V2\"`):\n- `MemberId` \u2014 the region segment is now `IdentityVersion.region(...)` = `\"V2\" + region` (e.g. `V2NSW26...`), so the whole member id (and its Luhn check digit) changes.\n- `OwnerIdentity.key` \u2014 the `\"V2\"` tag is folded into the hash input. Because it's a constant, two owners are still duplicates exactly when telephone/email/soundex match, so the 409 dedup semantics are preserved.\n- `Household.id` \u2014 the `\"V2\"` tag is folded into the hash input as a constant, so owners sharing a normalized last name + postcode still compute the *identical* householdId (grouping stays deterministic).\n\nEvery identifier changes, and since each mixes in the fixed tag, no version-1 value recurs. The tag lives **only inside** the identifiers.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` \u2192 generated DTO + `OwnerMapper`):\n- Added top-level `apiVersion: 2` (integer).\n- Added a nested `Identity` object grouping `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`; removed those three from the top level.\n- `locality`, `timezone`, and `ownerSegment` are untouched and keep the **plain** region code.\n\n**Audit event \u2192 schema version 2** (`AuditOwnerCreated`):\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` now serializes `{schemaVersion:2, seq, ownerId, memberId, ownerSegment, membershipLevel, event}` \u2014 added `schemaVersion` and the owner segment recomputed from the version-2 owner.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreV2GroupsIdentityAndVersions` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures). The audit log confirms the new shape:\n\n```\nAUDIT - {\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2716E6609E7\",\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nOne design note worth flagging: the task describes \"the region code used inside the identityKey and householdId,\" but in the existing code those two identifiers don't embed a region (only `memberId` does). I mixed the fixed `V2` **tag** (a constant) into their hash inputs rather than a city/postcode-derived region \u2014 deliberately, because folding in a variable region would have broken household grouping (when postcode is blank) and hard-duplicate detection (which must ignore region). This satisfies \"every identifier changes, no v1 value recurs\" while preserving those behaviors.",
