    "probe_text": "I've read the endpoint YAML and every function class in the pipeline (plus the DTO's bean-validation annotations and the telephone normalizer). Here is the complete ordered account of `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Failure \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler (403).\n\nAll 16 steps run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so persistence + all side-effects **commit once** at the end; any thrown escalation rolls back.\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `CheckIdempotentCreate`\n- Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key previously created an owner **and** that owner still exists \u2192 throws `IdempotentReplayException` carrying the existing owner (replays the original response instead of creating). No key / unseen key / vanished owner \u2192 falls through. *(Read-only lookup; no mutation.)*\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 `BuildOwner` (binds `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`)\nFirst, **bean validation** on the DTO (failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400):\n- `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n- `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern \u2026\\.?$`\n- `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n- `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n- `title` `@Size(\u226410)`, `address` `@Size(1,255)`, `addressLine1/2` `@Size(\u2264255)`, `email` `@Size(\u2264255)`, `postcode` `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`\n\nThen, in method body (side-effects + further validation):\n1. **Canonicalize address** \u2014 normalize `addressLine1/2`, compose the flat `address`, write all back onto the request.\n2. **Required-field check** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (non-empty after normalization), `city`, `telephone`; collects all missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n3. **Normalize telephone** to E.164 (`+61\u2026`, length-checked); invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n4. **Normalize email** \u2014 trim, syntactic regex check, lower-case; present-but-malformed \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400). Absent = allowed.\n5. **Map** DTO \u2192 `Owner`.\n6. **Registration date** \u2014 default to server date if null; **reject if in the future** \u2192 `RegistrationDateInFutureException` (400); then **roll forward** to the next business day (skips weekends + fixed 2026 holidays).\n7. **Stamp `memberId`** = `MemberId.of(owner)`.\n8. Publishes `Out<Owner>` and `Out<Boolean> sharesHousehold`.\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 `CheckOwnerEmailDomain`\n- If email present, reject disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400). No-op if absent.\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 `CheckOwnerPostcode`\n- If postcode present, re-check 4-digit format and the per-region range by city (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). No-op if absent or city has no known region.\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `AssignOwnerHousehold` *(side-effect only)*\n- Stamp deterministic `householdId` (first 12 hex of SHA-256 over normalized last name + postcode).\n- Stamp `householdSize` = self + existing owners sharing that `householdId`.\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`\n- Unless `sharesHousehold` is true: reject if the identity key (SHA-256 over normalized telephone, lower-cased email, Soundex of last name) equals any existing **non-deleted** owner's \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409). *(The only hard duplicate rejection.)*\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`\n- Reject if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409); otherwise **stamp `capacityWarning`** true when pre-existing count \u2265 40.\n\n## Step 8 \u2014 `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`\n- Reject if \u2265 100 owners already registered on this owner's (adjusted) `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n## Step 9 \u2014 `CheckOwnerBulkSignup` *(side-effect only)*\n- **Stamp `bulkSignupWarning`** true when > 80 owners already registered on that date.\n\n## Step 10 \u2014 `CountOwnerNamesakes` *(side-effect only)*\n- **Stamp `namesakeCount`** = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## Step 11 \u2014 `CheckOwnerPossibleDuplicate` *(side-effect only)*\n- Unless `sharesHousehold`, and only if postcode present: if an existing non-deleted owner has a different identity key but matching Soundex(lastName)+postcode, **stamp `possibleDuplicate`** true and **`possibleDuplicateOf`** = lowest matching id.\n\n## Step 12 \u2014 `DeduplicateMemberId` *(side-effect only)*\n- If `memberId` collides with an existing owner's, append `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) and re-stamp.\n\n## Step 13 \u2014 `CapOwnerMembershipLevel` *(side-effect only)*\n- Compute membership level and **cap at one above the max level among existing household members**; stamp `membershipLevel`.\n\n## Step 14 \u2014 `SaveOwner` *(side-effect)*\n- `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 persists and assigns the id. *(A DB constraint breach here \u2192 `DataIntegrityViolationException` handler.)*\n\n## Step 15 \u2014 `RecordIdempotentCreate` *(side-effect)*\n- Records `Idempotency-Key \u2192 owner.id` in the registry (no-op when no key).\n\n## Step 16 \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated` *(side-effect)*\n- Writes to the `AUDIT` logger: a human-readable line, plus a machine-readable `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event with a process-wide incrementing `seq`.\n\n## Step 17 \u2014 `EnqueueWelcomeNotification` *(side-effect)*\n- Writes a line to the `NOTIFY` logger (owner id + member id).\n\n## Step 18 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- Maps to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\nTwo things worth flagging as you read this:\n\n- **Ordering caveat:** the identity/uniqueness rejections (steps 6\u20138) run *after* the address/email/postcode format checks but the earlier steps 5, 9\u201313 already mutate the `owner` (household id/size, warnings, namesake count, member id, membership level). Because everything is one transaction, a rejection at step 6/7/8 rolls those back \u2014 but note steps 9\u201313 (warnings, dedupe, cap) run *after* the hard-reject checks, so their computation is only reached once the request is already accepted past the 409/429 gates.\n- **`sharesHousehold`** bypasses *both* the hard duplicate block (step 6) and the soft-duplicate flag (step 11), but not any other check.\n\nLet me know if you'd like the escalation-to-HTTP-status mapping for each exception verified against the handler YAMLs."
